# AI software-engineering loop

Understand the project → understand the requirement → smallest relevant context → smallest correct change → implement → verify → report concisely.

Priority: **Correctness > requirement > existing patterns > security/reliability > maintainability > token efficiency > short output.** Never skip understanding to save tokens.

## Do

- Read only what the task needs. Start at `package.json`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.agents/AGENTS.md`, and the matching file under `src/` or `docs/`. Do not scan the whole repo.
- Reuse `src/store`, `src/services`, `src/utils`, `src/components`. Prefer a small patch over a rewrite.
- Default scope is **webapp only**. Do not touch Android/iOS wrappers unless the user asks.
- Verify with the checks that match the change: `npm run lint`, a targeted Vitest file or `npm test`, `npm run build` when types/build matter. UI changes: exercise in the browser.
- Follow standing rules in `CLAUDE.md` (skill routing, bug/feature log before push, version bump) and `.agents/AGENTS.md` (ADRs, commit narrative, post-push cleanup).

## Do not

- Invent a new architecture, API, schema, or dependency when the existing one works.
- Re-read files already in context. Do not glob `**/*` “just in case”.
- Drive-by-refactor while fixing a bug.
- Dump a full project summary unless asked.

